  "delivered": [
    "An independent original embedding workbench now invokes all five selected native surfaces: filter_embeddings_top_k, to_embeddings, embedding_similarity on a supplied full EmbeddingResult, composed log-to-similarity, and embed_text. Original inputs are request-owned; no cached session or discovered replacement source is used.",
    "Native filtering returns the actual full EventLog, including all ten metadata members and complete stored Trace/Event/attribute state. Event-level keep_cases, duplicate and empty IDs, source order, zero-k filtering versus zero-k similarity, and exact native validation remain distinct. No internal embeddings or matches are fabricated for the filter result.",
    "All eight native value fields retain constructor defaults and supplied presence, literal string bytes, raw enum indexes, exact size_t and IEEE values. The ninth native callback member remains empty by default. A separate native_default/server integration selector can bind the actual immutable startup HTTP callback; unavailable explicit binding is an owned configuration error. HASHING remains the native provider default.",
    "An additional actual synthetic HTTP-provider proof exercised all five operations through registry-default and explicit server bindings, verified HASHING stayed unchanged, explicit callback versus native mock priority and zero-width inference, and retained every provider request/response. Its owned8570/8571 services were stopped while the existing8562/8568 processes stayed unchanged. This establishes HTTP/callback wiring with synthetic vectors; it does not establish a real transformer model.",
    "Caller raw logs, typed-table/import adapters and complete EmbeddingResult vectors remain separate from actual prepared logs/results. Complete ActiveEventSource snapshots retain actual source shape, all seventeen conversion options, typed origins, row ordinals, representative cells and projection changes. The native operations still consume their real EventLog signatures.",
    "Raw target/text inputs reach native string_view byte-for-byte, including empty, NUL, malformed UTF8 and WTF8. NativeString tags and versioned byte-safe raw-log/table/stream carriers preserve every stored public string without folding paired surrogate bytes. Full source/filtered raw-log and embedding-result artifacts reopen through the owned codecs.",
    "Original byte/SHA records, configured options, callback provenance, before/after snapshots, owned partial errors and actual native call records remain inspectable. All nine independent artifacts have authoritative bytecarriers; scalar-valid display text is optional, while actual legacy JSON/XES export failures remain separate from primary results. Reports, request/response, CSV and selected-record downloads retain full numeric and byte state.",
    "The UI provides all five operations, exact original uploads/text and source/import controls, full option and callback-binding editors, ownership/cancellation and complete result inspection. Actual native API captures drive frontend replay and export tests; omitted-control cases remain labelled offline evidence when the browser builder submits applicable defaults."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "This checkpoint does not establish full PM4Py parity or promote a strict unit. All 86 packages, 387 modules and 228 incomplete strict units remain in scope.",
    "A fresh actual browser retry was made for Feature65 after the user reported changing browser settings, while the coherent Feature64 server/PID23620 listened at8562. The browser still rejected access through its security policy. Current Feature65 native HTTP/API/assets are separate evidence; rendered layout, interaction and browser downloads remain unverified.",
    "Real host transformer/model availability and model-quality validation remain open unless a separate real-runtime proof establishes them. Hashing and the native explicit mock provider are labelled native behaviors; no model download, hidden mock substitution or fabricated callback transport is used. Unit callbacks establish member/registry/mock priority without claiming an actual host model.",
    "The final full API corpus reused PID16544 and began with the cache retained from historical attempt2. Its first request precedes only its own cache reseed; the historical fixture ID is not a fresh-empty-service claim. The earlier root five-operation smoke and historical attempt2 first filter before its initial seed separately establish uncached execution. Historical/smoke calls and synthetic-provider calls are excluded from the main final API totals; the cache-history audit also verifies exact downloaded raw-log reopen inputs.",
    "Source preparation may import a stream, dataframe or lazyframe before obtaining an actual checked EventLog; these are preparation adapters, not additional native embedding overloads. The full returned source and filtered logs remain authoritative even when an optional legacy export rejects otherwise stored state.",
    "Successful legacy artifacts can contain arbitrary native bytes, literal controls or text that is not parseable JSON. artifact_originals retains those bytes; a null display with no export error is a successful byte artifact. Full owned codecs and canonical byte-safe artifacts remain the reopening surfaces.",
    "Client cancellation prevents stale publication and does not stop an executing native call. Existing cached-log embedding operations remain available independently. The whole-catalogue inventory is historical static availability evidence, not behavioral or performance parity.",
    "The next bounded delivery is original weighted stochastic-language EMD, preserving existing log-derived EMD and its four host callback boundaries. Original object-centric playout, Table BOSE, independent original-source ILP/genetic discovery and every other recorded gap and strict gate remain open.",
    "Failed or superseded preparation, native build, API, export and frontend attempts remain retained and excluded from final successful counts."
